{
  "requirement": "Habeas's bundled agent instructions MUST direct agents to run Cargo doctests\nseparately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** `requirements.test-coverage.guidance.doctests` has one MUST. Habeas's bundled agent instructions must direct agents to run Cargo doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`. There are no boundary or failure cases to separate out.\n\n**Test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_default_to_process_coverage_and_keep_artifacts_disposable]` carries the `{test}` reference to this requirement. It checks the instruction text at three levels:\n- **Each skill's presence check.** For each of the `habeas`, `habeas-evidence` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements` skills, it builds the full skill text with `bundled_skill`. That text is the `SKILL.md` plus its reference files, whitespace-collapsed. It asserts that the text contains the literal `` `cargo test --doc --workspace` ``.\n- **The directive in context.** The `habeas` skill must contain \"Run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\". `habeas-evidence` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements` must contain \"run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\" in their \"Follow the habeas skill's …\" sentence.\n- **The SOP.** The bundled `agent-sops/approved-implementation.sop.md`, read with `include_str!`, must contain \"Run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\".\n\n**Why the assertions enforce the requirement.** The assertions are literal-phrase checks on the shipped instruction text. If a skill or the SOP dropped the doctest directive, or changed the command, the test would fail. The \"separately\" wording is asserted in each phrase, not only the command string. That is the whole content of the requirement.\n\n**Skills not asserted.** A search for the command found it in the `habeas`, `habeas-evidence` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements` skills and in the approved-implementation SOP. It also appears in the README, in `md/*` and in the `GUIDANCE` const in `src/execution_coverage.rs`. It is absent from the `habeas-requirements` skill, so the test has nothing to check there. The requirement speaks of the bundled instructions collectively. It does not require every skill to repeat the directive, so I do not treat this as a gap.\n\n**Verdict.** I found no untested obligation and no assertion that contradicts the requirement.",
